.nh
.TH "PB-TEAM-REMOVE" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-team-remove - Remove a team member


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb team remove <team> <account> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Remove a member from the team. Their team access and adopted defaults end at once.
Independently granted Git access and files or secrets they already received remain with them.
Pass the team's current generation with --generation (read it with pb team get). A stale
generation is rejected, so two people editing the team never overwrite each other.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--generation\fP=0
	expected current team generation

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for remove

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb team remove acme ana --generation 9
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-team(1)\fP
